    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm working on a doc for our new CI/CD pipeline. can u give me a quick breakdown of the main stages—code commit, automated testing, staging, and production—and specifically what kind of gates or checks we should have at each step to make sure nothing breaks?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For your CI/CD pipeline, the **Code Commit stage** should enforce static analysis (like linting), security scans, and unit tests before any automated builds occur. The **Automated Testing stage** needs integration and end-to-end tests with a strict build gate to ensure stability across services. At the **Staging stage**, implement deployment gates that validate environment parity, include a staged rollback plan, and verify no breaking changes reach live users. Finally, the **Production stage** requires feature flags or canary deployments to monitor performance metrics and error rates in real-time before full rollout. These gates collectively prevent regressions and minimize human error during deployment.",
      "source": "target",
