      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To truly protect your stakeholders, consider these critical red-flag gates within automated testing: a 40% or higher failure rate in unit tests, any regression in critical functional tests from the last stable release, and zero-passed security vulnerability scans. Additionally, a spike in memory leaks or severe performance degradation detected during the build simulation should trigger an immediate halt. If integration tests fail for over a continuous batch (e.g., 3 consecutive builds), the pipeline must stop and notify the team to investigate underlying environmental issues before proceeding to staging. Implementing these strict thresholds ensures that only stable, secure, and performant code reaches your production environment.",
